Shopify version of instasearch
----

Looks like this is a bug in instasearch **v1**, but not in **v2** as this works: 
 https://codesandbox.io/s/1rvmqq5jm4

But it does not work on my version. 


v2  {{ '//cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/instantsearch.js@2/dist/instantsearch.min.js' | script_tag }} 
v1  {{ '//cdn.jsdelivr.net/instantsearch.js/1/instantsearch.min.js' | script_tag }} 

Docs issue v1/v2
---
Docs for facetsExcludes say " Each facet must be properly defined in the facets attribute."
See https://community.algolia.com/algoliasearch-helper-js/reference.html#SearchParameters#facetsExcludes

but this works without  the facets attribute in v2 of instasearch :  https://codesandbox.io/s/1rvmqq5jm4


```
  searchParameters: {
    facetsExcludes: {
      brand: ["Sony"]
    },
    hitsPerPage: 8
  }

```

While this clearly is something that is going wrong, you can use `transformItems` to hide an item from a list, instead of doing it with helper parameters:

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.refinementList({
    container: '#brand-list',
    attributeName: 'brand',
    transformItems: items => items.filter(item => item.label !== 'Sony'),
  })
);
```

https://codesandbox.io/s/8k9wqo53pl?module=%2Fsrc%2Fapp.js

This is the workaround I see for v1:

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.refinementList({
    container: '#brand-list',
    attributeName: 'brand',
    // v2 version:
    // transformItems: items => items.filter(item => item.label !== 'Sony'),
    transformData: {
      item(item) {
        if (item.name === 'Sony') {
          // uses a bug in InstantSearch v1,
          // which will not add the classes on empty items
          return {};
        }
        return item;
      },
    },
  })
);
```

Then you can hide it with css:

```css
.ais-refinement-list--item label:not(.ais-refinement-list--label) {
  display: none;
}
```

